# entries[i].field = v in a loop, 48-byte elements: the index is scaled
# inline (i*48 = ((i<<1) + i) << 4), each field adds its offset to the
# scaled index, and each address, stored to a slot, is reloaded 2 bytes
# further up after the value's pha — the bug this fixture was written for
# gave the first iteration wrong offsets after a push. No original check
# existed (opensnes-emu only compiled it). Offsets are today's frame layout
# (moved by the slot colouring of 2026-09-27, which also reuses the loop
# variable's slot for the scaled index once i is dead in the body):
# if they move, re-derive "reload = store + 2" before updating.
in init_with_loop: present sta\.b tcc__r9\n\tasl a\n\tclc\n\tadc\.b tcc__r9\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tsta(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)
in init_with_loop: absent __mul16
# Since 2026-10-08 each field is written with indexed-long addressing: X is
# the scaled index, the field offset is in the operand, no value is pushed.
in init_with_loop: present tax\n\tlda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tsta\.l entries,x
# ...and X is loaded once for the four fields (the X cache, same day).
in init_with_loop: present tax\n\tlda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tsta\.l entries,x\n\tlda\.w #100\n\tsta\.l entries\+2,x\n\tlda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tsta\.l entries\+4,x\n\tlda\.w #16\n\tsta\.l entries\+6,x
in init_with_loop: absent pha
# x = 64 + i*16.
in init_with_loop: present lda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tasl a\n\tclc\n\tadc\.w #64\n
# The unrolled twin: element k at entries + 48k.
in init_without_loop: present lda\.w #80\n\tsta\.w entries\+48\n[\s\S]*lda\.w #16\n\tsta\.w entries\+150\n
